WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight i
Tony- and Academy Award-winnin

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:05.171
actress who you know from film
like "Chicago" and "Traffic.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
She stars in the series
"Prodigal Son,"

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
which airs Tuesday nights
on Fox.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
Catherine Zeta-Jones.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hello, Catherine.
How are you?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:14.714 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm good, Seth.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so lovely to see you.
It's been a while.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.084 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It has been awhile.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a delight
to see you.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
How have you and your family
been holding up?

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.724 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Pretty good, you know?

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:28.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's been
an unprecedented year

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.863 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for everybody.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
I must say, personally,
it was lovely

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we were in a vulnerable
and unknowing time

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have my peeps,
my loved ones around.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I had my son home
from college

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my daughter home
from school.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
She goes to school
in Switzerland.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we were all back
in our bubble.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:51.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
And supposedly,
speaking to my son,

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
we fared better
than many families.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Mom,
you don't understand --

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
people aren't talking
to each other."

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.525 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're like, "No."

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.060 line:92%
So, we played lots of games.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
My kids -- and I must say,
kudos to them.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought for sure, you know
they're all back --

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:09.235
not just them, but all their
other friends from high school

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.637 line:92%
all live down our street, right?

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were brought up right her
all together.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought it was gonna b
party central.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.143
You know, all these kids
coming back from college,

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
congregating in
the garage band garage,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.848 size:81% position:41% line:92%
which is usually ours.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.684 size:84% position:42%
But they really got it.
So, we had a good time.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.754
And they're finishing up now and
looking forward to, hopefully,

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:31.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
a more kind of outdoorsy summe
than we had last year.

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:32.792 line:92%
-Well, that is a credit to them.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you feel a sympathy
for the fact that, you know,

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.499
they were young people who were,
in your son's case,

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
losing a year
of in-person college?

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
I live vicariously
through my kids.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me tell you.
I never went to college.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was schlepping the board
of London and that,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
touring "The Pajama Game"
at 15 --

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
jazz hands, jazz hands,
jazz hands.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.184 size:78% position:39%
You know, so there is
a part of me that --

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.120 line:92%
I mean, I had an education

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.190
but I self-educated myself in my
love for learning, you know.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.393
And so my kids -- who got
all their brains from me,

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.761 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but don't tell Michael.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.463 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know? I mean...

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:13.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I just read
a wonderful article.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:16.503
I didn't quite appreciate
how young you started.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:20.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
You mentioned your early
schlepping across the boards

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you knew
at a very young age,

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
as soon as you got
a taste of it,

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this would be
what you were gonna do.

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, I was --

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
They did this big publicit
stunt in Britain

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:32.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
looking for kids for "Annie,
and then subsequently,

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
Micky Dolenz's directorial
"Bugsy Malone" onstage.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Right?

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.993 line:92%
So they came to Wales, they...

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they went down
to my --

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where I live in Wales
is the end of the track.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't go further west
unless you get the Cork ferr

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.234 line:92%
over to Ireland, you know?

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.304
So they came down in a publicity
stunt, basically.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:55.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so me, who had aspirations
and was in dance school

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the church hall down th
street, you know,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:02:59.679 size:88% position:44% line:92%
auditioned and I got it.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:04.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was the spark,
you know, that got me into

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:08.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
this amazing -- I'm humbly
grateful -- business

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it's just taken me
on this wild journey.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:13.927
But my kids who are in college
who I live vicariously through

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:17.864
you know, it's like, they can'
do what they're supposed to do

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:18.831 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know, it's like...

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, I used to say to my
kids, you know,

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:23.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they called me on a Saturda
morning, if it was early,

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd go, "why are you still -
why are you awake?

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Shouldn't you be, like,
sleeping?

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
What time did you get home
last night?"

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.477 line:92%
"Oh, I was in bed by 10:00."

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Are you crazy?!"

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:33.580 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:36.950
"You worked so hard throug
the week and you're in bed?!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.218 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What's wrong with you?

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.986 line:92%
What's wrong with you, son?"

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.054 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So anyway, they do --

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
they love learning and
they're having a great time.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I kind of lost
that part of my life.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:49.529
Not that I'm complaining, 'cause
I wouldn't be speaking to you,

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.297 line:92%
which I always love to do.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:57.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I love to see them be
teenagers and just, you know

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:01.441
and excited to see where
their journey takes them.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:04.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they both
love learning,

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they both are very goo
young actors.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've never done anythin
professional

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
or anything like that,
but as actors,

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:14.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
both my husband and I, Michael
you know, we...

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are so many other
professions

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.057 line:92%
that we'd like them to be in

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.726 line:92%
But it's very, very clear

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they've got
that fire in their belly.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:25.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for me, it's like,
"Party on, guys,"

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's just taken me
on a great journey.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:32.038
But I was never the son of
Spartacus like Michael was

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:32.572 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure, yeah.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:34.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that's a different
kettle of fish.

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a different bear,
babe, you know?

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:40.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so even with that,
those reservations,

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
but clearly, Michael had t
prove himself

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.452 line:92%
maybe more than the average bear

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
because his dad was
Kirk Douglas.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, even with that
deterrent,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're like,
"Nah, still love it."

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:56.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do -- Obviously, they hav
two actors for parents,

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
but maybe you are the only
accomplished dancer.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.769
I'm not quite sure where Michael
falls on the dancing scale

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm gonna say
it's safe to say

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.006
you're the better of the two
-Did you ever see the video?

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.643 line:92%
♪♪ When the going gets tough

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.811 line:92%
That's as good as it gets, babe.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:15.381 size:84% position:42%
It's like, he can click
in time to the beat.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.117 size:75% position:38%
Every now and again,
he gets off course.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.752 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But he's a great actor.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
Michael always says that
when you're dancing,

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Always look at me
from the waist up."

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because he can do the...
